\caption(The actual tensor graph and complete parameter census. The selector has its own source-ID branch; only four patches enter the encoder and the decoder restores sixteen locations.)
\alttext(A branched tensor architecture shows a source-ID selector joining image patches, selected positions, restored projected codes and hidden tokens. The encoder handles four tokens; the decoder predicts sixteen patches.)

For width w, the attention matrices contribute 4w², the two feed-forward matrices 4w²,
feed-forward biases 3w, and three LayerNorms (including the final norm) 6w. Thus each
block/final-norm group has 8w²+9w scalars: 8,480 for the encoder and 2,192 for the decoder.
Patch embedding adds 1,600, decoder projection 528, mask token 16 and prediction head 833:
1,600 + 8,480 + 528 + 16 + 2,192 + 833 = 13,649.

> Genuine MNIST and source provenance

The canonical dataset preparation loads the original balanced pools: 1,000 fitting, 200
validation and 200 test images, Float32 [N,28,28,1] in [0,1]. Fitting and validation use disjoint
official training IDs; held-out records come from the official test split. The provenance
manifest and all source IDs are retained. Labels select gallery columns only.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", cache.string());
  const auto      pools = n::models::LoadSaliency(cache / "saliency");
  n::NamedTensors data;
  std::print("| pool | images | per digit | hidden pixels per image |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int split = 0; split < 3; ++split) {
    const std::string name = split == 0 ? "fit" : split == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    data.emplace_back(name + "_images", pools[split].images);
    data.emplace_back(name + "_source_ids", pools[split].source);
    data.emplace_back(name + "_labels", pools[split].labels);
    std::print(
        "| {} | {} | {} | 588 |\n",
        name,
        pools[split].images.size(0),
        pools[split].images.size(0) / 10);
  }
  n::save_npz("build/masked_data.npz", data);
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      cache / "saliency" / "manifest.json",
      "build/masked_data_manifest.json",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
}
```
